 # The agent loop
+
+The agent loop is a fundamental concept in building an AI agent, where the model continuously interacts with tools based on its decisions until a task is completed. It operates in a cycle, where the model generates responses, decides on actions, and invokes tools to achieve its goals. The loop continues until the model determines that it has finished the task, at which point it calls a specific tool to signal completion.
+
+In essence, the agent loop consists of a series of interactions between the user, the language model (LLM), and the tools available to the agent. The LLM decides what actions to take, while the harness manages how those actions are executed, ensuring a structured and controlled workflow throughout the process.
 
 The most important concept in the entire project is the agent loop.
 
